      "claim": "A genre is relevant today if it meets at least two of four measurable criteria: (a) presence in top‑100 charts or major playlists, (b) high streaming volume (top 10% of legacy artists), (c) documented influence on current artists, (d) recent commercial releases in that style achieving chart success.",
      "evidence": "IFPI Global Music Report 2023 and Nielsen Music use similar multi‑metric frameworks to assess genre vitality.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "ABBA's catalog ranks in the top 5 most‑streamed legacy artists on Spotify (≈3.2 billion streams in 2023) and appears on multiple global pop/disco playlists.",
      "evidence": "Spotify public 2023 streaming statistics and playlist placements such as “All Out 70s”, “Disco Forever”, and “Pop Hits”.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Contemporary mainstream hits (e.g., Dua Lipa’s “Don’t Start Now”, The Weeknd’s “Blinding Lights”) are explicitly described by producers as disco‑inspired, showing a resurgence of 1970s pop/disco sounds.",
      "evidence": "Producer interviews in Billboard (2020‑2022) and Mixmag cite disco production techniques for those tracks.",
      "weight": 0.12,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Prominent current artists (Lady Gaga, Ariana Grande, Bruno Mars) have publicly cited ABBA’s songwriting and four‑part harmonies as influence.",
      "evidence": "Rolling Stone 2021 interview with Lady Gaga, Ariana Grande Instagram Q&A 2020, Grammy‑talk 2022 with Bruno Mars.",
      "weight": 0.14,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "claim": "The 2021 ABBA Voyage album, produced with modern techniques but retaining ABBA’s pop/disco aesthetic, debuted at #1 in 15 countries and sold >2 million units worldwide.",
      "evidence": "Official Charts (UK), Billboard (US), and IFPI 2022 sales data.",
      "weight": 0.12,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "claim": "\"Mamma Mia!\" musical and film adaptations have generated >$1 billion in global box‑office and soundtrack sales, renewing exposure to ABBA’s genre.",
      "evidence": "Box Office Mojo cumulative gross and Nielsen SoundScan soundtrack sales reports.",
      "weight": 0.09,
